Spec: Project/Domains

Purpose:
  Defines the business domains represented in the project â€” schema only,
   not a concrete domain list.

Rules:
  Each domain MUST have an identifiable owner.
  Domain knowledge MUST remain within its own domain model.
  Cross-domain dependencies MUST be explicit (see dependencies.sdd).

Note:
  This differs from the module-level concept in map.sdd: `modules.sdd`
   describes the technical/code-boundary contract (owns/api/deps), this
   file is the schema of the business-domain model â€” in practice they
   often 1:1 match (e.g. "payment" can be both a module and a domain),
   but conceptually they are separate and must not be mixed.

   (prompt/new/21.md, STEP 4) The old `map.sdd` version mixed these two
   concepts by repeating the module list in the "Domains:" section (see
   map.sdd -> Note). This file was created to separate that confusion.
   Concrete domains (payment, course, user, etc.) will be rebuilt
   according to this schema in a future "next" step.


